AOT code caches: guest RIPs from data slots, exit linker via the thread state (FEX 14c9268)

New option AOTCodeCacheWIP (only affects code cache generation). With it:
- Guest RIP constants are loaded with adrp + ldr from a data slot instead of
  a 4-instruction move that is patched on load. The adrp/ldr immediates are
  resolved when the cache is serialized; the data area sits at a fixed
  distance after the code (aligned to 16 KiB) and holds one slot per
  RELOC_GUEST_RIP_DATA_SLOT relocation, in relocation order. The loader
  maps it read-write next to the code and fills it in; the code is not
  touched.
- Jump thunks load the exit function linker from
  CpuStateFrame::Pointers.ExitFunctionLinker instead of a per-block literal,
  so EXITFUNCTION_LINKER relocations disappear.

